  "description": "The Adolf Munkel Weg is an easy 6 km footpath that traverses beneath the Odle / Geisler rock walls in the Dolomites, between roughly 1,860 and 2,050 m, with only 350 m of total ascent. OpenStreetMap rates it mountain hiking (SAC T2) — no technical sections are tagged. A spring (Weißbrunn / Fontana Bianca) and the Brogleshütte hut (2,047 m) are mapped on the route.\n\nRoute data © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). OSM relation/2442695.\nCover photo: Matthias Bethke / CC BY-SA 4.0 / Wikimedia Commons.",
